// Remote sensing (PRD §7.2, D18). Rust rolls one skill check per fidelity layer; this slot sets
// the difficulty of each tile: `distance` in tiles from the party, `visibility` the visibility
// depth of the party's tile (the environment's light), `layer` 1 terrain, 2 structure, 3 objects,
// 4 creatures. Tiles the eye already reaches are DC 10; each tile past the visibility depth adds
// one; each layer above terrain adds two. Cover and concealment become inputs with objects and
// monsters.
//
// Sight from a height (M8.5): `sight_rise_per_tile` is how far, in eighths of a cell (a wall is
// 8), the party must stand above the lowest tile around it to see one tile farther; 0 turns it
// off. Hills hiding what lies behind them is not a rule: it is the geometry.
(
    schema: 1,
    id: "base:rules:sensing",
    values: {"sight_rise_per_tile": 8},
    slots: {
        "sense.dc": (inputs: ["distance", "visibility", "layer"], expr: "10 + max(0, distance - visibility) + (layer - 1) * 2"),
    },
)
